Uptime Kuma is a fancy, self-hosted, and open-source monitoring tool used to track the availability and health of your websites, APIs, databases, and servers. It features an intuitive, fast user interface and alerts you immediately when services go down.
Core Features 

* Monitor Anything: Track HTTP/HTTPS websites, TCP/UDP ports, DNS records, SSL certificates, Docker containers, and cron jobs. 
* Instant Notifications: Receive alerts through dozens of integrated channels, including Discord, Slack, Telegram, email, and webhooks. 
* Status Pages: Create beautiful, customizable, public or private status pages to keep your users or clients informed of service outages. 
* Responsive Dashboard: View real-time status, historical uptime percentages, and response latency graphs in a clean layout. 

